वा
वा vā, encl. pcl. or (following, but metr. sts. 🞄preceding);<BR> either or not, optionally;<BR> (= 🞄iva), like, as, as it were;<BR> (= eva), just, etc. 🞄(rare);<BR> but, however (rare);<BR> even, even supposing 🞄(with ft.;<BR> rare);<BR> after inter. or rel. = 🞄possibly, pray: vā — vā, either — or (when 🞄there are two clauses, the vb. of the first only 🞄is as a rule accented);<BR> na ± vā — vā, kiṃ 🞄vā — kiṃ vā or na vā, neither — nor;<BR> vā — 🞄na vā, either — or not;<BR> perhaps — or perhaps 🞄not;<BR> whether — or not;<BR> yadi-vā-vā, whether 🞄— or;<BR> in a sentence containing more than two 🞄members vā is nearly always repeated, while 🞄a negative at the beginning of the series need 🞄not be repeated as its sense runs through all 🞄the remaining members (= not, either — or — 🞄or);<BR> in this case vā often interchanges with 🞄ca and api, or is combined with the pcls.. api 🞄(± punaḥ), atha (± u, api, or punaḥ), yad, 🞄yadi, or utá.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MD&page=274-3" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=md" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वा
