containing Soma, 🞄attended etc. by Soma (V.);<BR> -vallī, f. Soma 🞄plant;<BR> -vāra, m. Monday;<BR> -vāsara, m. or 🞄n. id.;<BR> -vikrayin, a. selling Soma;<BR> m. seller 🞄of Soma;<BR> -vṛddha, pp. invigorated by Soma 🞄(RV.);<BR> -śarman, m. N. of a various men;<BR> 🞄(sóma) -śita, pp. sharpened by Soma;<BR> -śnṣman, m. N. (Br.);<BR> -śūra, m. N.;<BR> -saṃsthā, 🞄f. fundamental form of the Soma sacrifice;<BR> 🞄-sad, m. pl. N. of the Manes of the Sādhyas;<BR> 🞄-salila, n. Soma water;<BR> -sú-t, a. pressing 🞄Soma;<BR> -suta, m. son or descendant of the 🞄Moon;<BR> (sóma) -suti, f. pressing of Soma;<BR> 🞄-sūtvan, a. pressing Soma;<BR> m. Soma-presser;<BR> 🞄-svāmin, m. N.;<BR> -ānanda, m. N.;<BR> āraudrá, a. belonging to Soma and Rudra;<BR> 🞄n. (sc. sūkta) the hymn RV. VI, 74 (C.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=MD&page=360-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=md" target="_blank">Correction</a>

